---
import '../styles/global.css';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import me from '../images/me.png';
import spotInsight from '../images/SpotInsight.jpg';
const email = 'mailto:David.GuerreroD@protonmail.com';
const services = [
  ['01', 'Document & PDF tools', 'Turn information into useful documents.', 'Custom forms, document builders, live previews and PDF exports that fit the way you work.'],
  ['02', 'Workflow integrations', 'Make your tools work together.', 'Connect forms, APIs and existing systems to reduce repetitive handoffs and keep information moving.'],
  ['03', 'Small web projects', 'Build a focused, useful web experience.', 'Clear websites, practical dashboards and compact web apps, designed around one well-defined need.'],
];
const steps = [
  ['Scope', 'We talk through the problem, the people using the tool and what a useful first version needs to do.'],
  ['Build', 'I turn the agreed scope into a working version, with progress you can see and try.'],
  ['Review', 'We walk through real use cases, refine the details and check the experience on relevant devices.'],
  ['Handover', 'You get the finished work and practical guidance on how to use and maintain it.'],
];
---
<Layout title="David Guerrero | Custom tools for small businesses" description="Custom document and PDF tools, workflow integrations, and focused web projects for small businesses. Explore David Guerrero’s work and discuss your project.">
  <main id="main">
    <section class="container hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Independent web developer</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">Custom tools for the way your business works</h1>
        <p class="lede">Less busywork. A smoother workflow. I build practical web tools for small businesses, from document generators to connected systems.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href={email}>Discuss a project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#projects">Explore my work <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
        <p class="hero-note">A focused scope. Direct collaboration. Thoughtful delivery.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="hero-visual">
        <div class="visual-top"><span class="visual-dots" aria-hidden="true">● ● ●</span><span>Project spotlight / ResuEase</span></div>
        <img src="/resuease-brand.png" width="1200" height="630" alt="ResuEase’s original branded visual: Build your professional resume" fetchpriority="high" />
        <figcaption><div><strong>From structured data to a finished PDF</strong><span>Personal project · Resume builder</span></div><a href="#resuease" aria-label="Read the ResuEase case study">↗</a></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <section id="services" class="container section" aria-labelledby="services-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">What I can help with</p><h2 id="services-title">Small tools.<br />Useful changes.</h2><p>You don’t always need a huge platform. Sometimes you need one part of your day to work better.</p></div>
      <div class="service-grid">{services.map(([number, title, intro, detail]) => <article class="service-card"><span class="number">{number}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p class="service-intro">{intro}</p><p>{detail}</p></article>)}</div>
    </section>
    <section id="projects" class="container section" aria-labelledby="work-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Selected personal projects</p><h2 id="work-title">The thinking behind the work.</h2><p>Self-directed projects that show how I approach useful interfaces, structured data and integrations.</p></div>
      <article id="resuease" class="case-study featured">
        <div class="case-heading"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Documents & PDFs</p><h3>ResuEase</h3><p class="case-summary">A resume builder that brings editing, preview and export into one workflow.</p><div class="tags"><span>React</span><span>React-PDF</span><span>PDF.js</span><span>Supabase</span></div></div>
        <div class="case-detail"><h4>The problem</h4><p>Resume content needs to stay editable while the final document keeps a consistent layout. A preview is only useful if it matches the file you download.</p><h4>The approach</h4><p>Structured forms, reorderable sections and local autosave support the editing flow. Browser-side React-PDF generates the document; PDF.js renders the preview. Preview and download share the generated PDF artifact, replacing the previous Puppeteer-based export path.</p><h4>What it demonstrates</h4><p>A document workflow that connects user input to a downloadable output, with PDF generation handled locally in the browser. This is a personal project, not commissioned client work.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="https://resuease.vercel.app/">Open ResuEase ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/DavidGD616/ResuEase">View source ↗</a></div><p class="small-note">The live app starts at sign-in. The hero uses the project’s existing branded image, rather than an editor screenshot.</p></div>
      </article>
      <article class="case-study secondary">
        <div class="project-image"><Image src={spotInsight} alt="Existing SpotInsight project screenshot showing its Spotify listening-data interface" loading="lazy" /><p class="small-note">Existing project screenshot · Personal project</p></div>
        <div class="case-detail"><p class="eyebrow">02 / API integration</p><h3>SpotInsight</h3><p class="case-summary">Making personal listening data easier to explore.</p><h4>The approach</h4><p>A React interface with an Express backend brings together Spotify listening data: top artists, tracks and recent plays. Playlist recommendations extend the experience from viewing information to acting on it.</p><h4>What it demonstrates</h4><p>Connecting an external API to a focused interface and turning several data views into a coherent user experience. This personal project runs locally; it is not presented as a live production service.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/DavidGD616/spotinsight">Explore the source ↗</a></div>
      </article>
    </section>
    <section id="process" class="container section" aria-labelledby="process-title"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">How we’ll work</p><h2 id="process-title">Clear steps, from idea to handover.</h2></div><ol class="process-grid">{steps.map(([title, description], index) => <li><span class="number">0{index + 1}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></li>)}</ol></section>
    <section id="about-me" class="container section about" aria-labelledby="about-title"><Image src={me} width={180} alt="Portrait of David Guerrero" loading="lazy" /><div><p class="eyebrow">The person behind the code</p><h2 id="about-title">Hi, I’m David.</h2><p>My interest in development started with an e-commerce business in 2019. The business didn’t work out, but building it sparked a lasting interest in solving problems with software.</p><p>I’m a self-taught developer working with JavaScript, React and Next.js. I like turning complicated tasks into clear, usable web experiences—and working directly with the people who need them.</p></div></section>
    <section id="contact" class="container contact section" aria-labelledby="contact-title"><p class="eyebrow">Let’s start with the problem</p><h2 id="contact-title">What would make your<br />workday easier?</h2><p>Tell me what you’re trying to do, what feels clunky and what you already use. We can work out a sensible next step together.</p><a class="button primary" href={email}>Discuss a project ↗</a><a class="email-link" href={email}>David.GuerreroD@protonmail.com</a></section>
  </main>
</Layout>
